        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "fcb2b7fd-73d9-5478-9571-c136eabe5527",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris DeStefano, Brett Eldredge, Terry Eldredge, Carrie Underwood, Billy Currington, Luke Bryan, Miranda Lambert, Rascal Flatts, Jason Aldean\n- Places: Mt. Laurel, New Jersey, Nashville, Tennessee\n- Products: “Good Girl,” “Little Toy Guns,” “Hey Girl,” “Don't Ya,” “That's My Kind of Night,” “Kick the Dust Up,” “Somethin' Bad,” “Rewind,” “Just Gettin' Started,” “Beat of the Music,” “Mean to Me,” Bring You Back\n- Organizations: The Grascals, Billboard Country Airplay, NBC Sunday Night Football\n- Roles: singer-songwriter, record producer, multi-instrumentalist\n\nFacts:\n- Chris DeStefano is a Grammy Award-winning American singer-songwriter, record producer, and multi-instrumentalist who was raised in Mt. Laurel, New Jersey, and lives in Nashville, Tennessee.\n- Chris DeStefano wrote multiple No. 1 songs, including Carrie Underwood’s “Good Girl” and “Little Toy Guns,” Billy Currington’s “Hey Girl,” Brett Eldredge’s “Don't Ya,” Luke Bryan’s “That's My Kind of Night” and “Kick the Dust Up,” Rascal Flatts’ “Rewind,” and Jason Aldean’s “Just Gettin' Started.”\n- Chris DeStefano co-wrote “Somethin' Bad” for Miranda Lambert and Carrie Underwood, and that song was later reworked as the opening theme for NBC Sunday Night Football.\n- Brett Eldredge is the cousin of Terry Eldredge of The Grascals.\n- Brett Eldredge had three No. 1 singles on the Billboard Country Airplay chart from his debut studio album Bring You Back: “Don't Ya,” “Beat of the Music,” and “Mean to Me.”",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5b8e51e1-7350-552a-ab9d-1a7b3f9653a7",
        "text": "Page: Chris DeStefano. Sentence: Christopher Michael \"Chris\" DeStefano is a Grammy Award Winning American singer/songwriter, record producer and multi instrumentalist, raised in Mt. Laurel, New Jersey and currently residing in Nashville, Tennessee.\nPage: Chris DeStefano. Sentence: As a songwriter, he has multiple #1 songs with artists Carrie Underwood (“Good Girl”, \"Little Toy Guns\"), Billy Currington (“Hey Girl”), Brett Eldredge (\"Don't Ya\"), Luke Bryan (\"That's My Kind of Night\", \"Kick the Dust Up\" ), Miranda Lambert & Carrie Underwood (\"Somethin' Bad,\" later reworked as the opening theme for \"NBC Sunday Night Football\"), Rascal Flatts (\"Rewind\") and Jason Aldean (\"Just Gettin' Started\").\nPage: Brett Eldredge. Sentence: The cousin of Terry Eldredge of The Grascals, Eldredge has had three No. 1 singles on the \"Billboard\" Country Airplay chart from his debut studio album, \"Bring You Back\": \"Don't Ya\", \"Beat of the Music\", and \"Mean to Me\".",
